From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:27:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] x11stereochildren: Show a declared child only where X
 shows it

A declared X11 child is redirected, so Xwayland gives it a surface whose buffer
is whole, and the scene drew all of it at the child's place. A child larger than
its window showed outside the window, and a window stacked over the child (a
sibling mapped after it) was hidden by it, where the X server draws the child
clipped to its window and the windows between, and hides it under any viewable
window stacked over it.

X11StereoChild::visible is the X11 window's area, cut to the windows between it
and the child, less the bounding shapes (SHAPE, border included) of the viewable
windows stacked over the child or over a window between, found with
xcb_query_tree. Declared children are left to the scene's order.
SurfaceItemXwaylandChild::shapeForSourceBox(), which both eyes' quads and
shape() are built from, is cut to it in the item's own coordinates, so the view
is cut once whatever the child's place or scale, and a child that fits its
window with nothing over it is unchanged.

The covering windows are watched, not polled: the X11 window and the windows
between it and the child select SubstructureNotify (the X11 window's own event
mask is kept), Workspace::workspaceEvent hands the Create, Destroy, Map, Unmap,
Reparent, Configure and Circulate events of their children to the child's owner,
a covering window's ShapeNotify is selected on the window itself, and the area
follows the X11 window's size.

